1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,944
Online shopping has a conversation problem.

2
00:00:02,944 --> 00:00:08,216
Filter walls make you translate what
you want into someone else's categories.

3
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:10,270
AI assistants do the opposite,

4
00:00:10,270 --> 00:00:14,104
interrogating you for ten
turns before showing anything.

5
00:00:14,104 --> 00:00:18,417
Both burn the one thing shoppers
will not give twice: patience.

6
00:00:18,417 --> 00:00:22,017
So we stopped optimizing
how our agent ranks products,

7
00:00:22,017 --> 00:00:25,951
and started optimizing when it
knows enough to rank at all.

8
00:00:25,951 --> 00:00:31,551
Every turn resolves one question: is
another question worth more than another guess?

9
00:00:31,551 --> 00:00:36,951
Modelling that value-of-information
decision explicitly is our core contribution.

10
00:00:36,951 --> 00:00:40,285
It converges in under
three turns, at zero tokens.

11
00:00:40,285 --> 00:00:45,976
Five deterministic stages. Dialogue
state tracks slots and intent overrides.

12
00:00:45,976 --> 00:00:49,794
An exact-evidence
conjunction builds the hard pool.

13
00:00:49,794 --> 00:00:54,886
The value-of-information
controller then decides: ask, or recommend.

14
00:00:54,886 --> 00:00:57,881
Ranking is popularity-first late fusion,

15
00:00:57,881 --> 00:01:02,448
with a local MiniLM encoder
adding a small cosine adjustment.

16
00:01:02,448 --> 00:01:06,192
The optional language
model rerank ships disabled.

17
00:01:06,192 --> 00:01:11,380
This is the organizers' own
simulator — no mock-up, no website.

18
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:16,239
Session public zero zero two,
the Intent Override scenario.

19
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:20,609
Turn one. The customer wants
a belt with a buckle closure.

20
00:01:20,609 --> 00:01:24,075
That matches two hundred fifty-eight products,

21
00:01:24,075 --> 00:01:28,972
so the agent withholds the list
entirely and asks about material.

22
00:01:28,972 --> 00:01:35,708
Turn two. Leather is disclosed and the hard
pool collapses from two hundred fifty-eight to

23
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:39,076
twenty-two. A weaker agent would answer here.

24
00:01:39,076 --> 00:01:42,818
Ours calculates that one
more question still wins.

25
00:01:42,818 --> 00:01:46,206
Turn three: the customer changes their mind.

26
00:01:46,206 --> 00:01:51,981
The state replaces the old preference
instead of appending a contradiction,

27
00:01:51,981 --> 00:01:55,215
and any hit scored before it is discarded.

28
00:01:55,215 --> 00:02:00,934
Turn four. Two more attributes
arrive, the hard pool drops to seven,

29
00:02:00,934 --> 00:02:05,476
and the controller decides
the evidence is sufficient.

30
00:02:05,476 --> 00:02:10,438
It recommends — and the target
belt comes back at rank one.

31
00:02:10,438 --> 00:02:15,621
That is the whole idea: ask while
the answer would change the ranking,

32
00:02:15,621 --> 00:02:18,065
and stop the moment it would not.

33
00:02:18,065 --> 00:02:22,005
The weak baseline finds the
target twelve percent of the time.

34
00:02:22,005 --> 00:02:24,547
We find it every time on the public set,

35
00:02:24,547 --> 00:02:27,407
at a technical score of zero point nine five.

36
00:02:27,407 --> 00:02:32,110
But the number we actually trust is
this one: across eight hundred unseen,

37
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,953
identifier-disjoint sessions,

38
00:02:33,953 --> 00:02:39,037
our stopping controller delivered sixty
additional rank-one recommendations with

39
00:02:39,037 --> 00:02:42,786
zero Hit-rate loss, improving
on all eight of eight shards.

40
00:02:42,786 --> 00:02:48,784
Zero marginal inference cost means
this deploys at marketplace scale,

41
00:02:48,784 --> 00:02:50,088
not demo scale.

42
00:02:50,088 --> 00:02:56,609
It runs offline on commodity CPU, so
no shopping intent leaves the process.

43
00:02:56,609 --> 00:02:59,999
And the controller is catalog agnostic.
